+## Methods, uncertainty, false positives and missing measurements (to Parliament)
+
+- **Sampling.** n=4 from a frozen 502-item universe; no prevalence, trend or "whole board is healthy"
+  inference is possible. Populations differ, so verdict types are not comparable across rows. The
+  draw is reproducible from the stored seed/snapshot but was not known from a public timestamp.
+- **Verified vs leading indicators.** Only directly fetched board state, GitHub API merge/PR fields,
+  Git ancestry/exact-commit suite carriers, and file existence are treated as verified. Agent
+  liveness, `[scheduler-turn]`/`state: working`/`state: delivered` lines, prompt counts and self-reported
+  byte/hash figures are leading indicators, not delivery or host telemetry. An agent being alive or
+  writing a report was not counted as useful delivery.
+- **False-positive risks.** Host assignments here rest on agent self-reports and author labels, not
+  telemetry; the scheduler quotes the billy-dev-only policy itself, which raises, not lowers, confidence
+  in case 1's finding but does not supply direct host observation. Case 2's verified verdict rests on
+  GitHub API merge fields plus the board review object, not a re-run of the tool or a read of every
+  explicit state. Case 4's gate record is an integrator artifact; it evidences the recorded gate, not a
+  fresh test run. Absence of a finding is not a clean bill of health.
+- **Missing measurements.** No marceline-dev host telemetry; no authenticated access to private
+  external repos (skrynia-apps#210 returned 404); no local re-run of the Ivanka or Antonina test
+  suites; no live deployment/boot verification for case 4; no independent confirmation of the
+  integration reviewer's seat identity; no full acceptance review of the fail-closed decision tool.
+  These are reported as limitations, **not** as clean results.
+- **Observed measurement weakness (described, not reformed).** Activity and self-attestation continue
+  to coexist with unverified outcomes and absent telemetry (cases 1 and 2). The Judiciary describes
+  this for legislative consideration and proposes, sponsors, ratifies and implements no change to
+  measurement systems, audit algorithms, institutional rules or its own operation (Act 15 §2).
